Data Sources, Usage Restrictions, and Ethical Considerations
Data Sources

The Military Hidden Human Dataset (HuCOD) was constructed using a combination of:

publicly available camouflage and camouflaged human datasets;
images collected from publicly accessible internet sources;

No classified, confidential, proprietary, or restricted military imagery was used in the construction of this dataset.

Annotation Procedure

Images were manually reviewed and annotated to identify camouflaged human targets as already defined in publicly avialable images.
images with not such data has been manually reviewed and anotations are made avialable.

Intended Use

This dataset is provided solely for:

academic research;
educational purposes;
benchmarking and evaluation of camouflaged object detection and segmentation algorithms.

The dataset is not intended for operational military deployment, surveillance activities, or other applications requiring certified real-world performance.

Redistribution and Licensing

The HuCOD dataset contains images originating from multiple publicly available sources. Copyright ownership remains with the respective original creators and dataset providers. Users are responsible for complying with the licensing terms and usage restrictions associated with the original sources.

Where redistribution restrictions apply, only annotations, metadata, image identifiers, and experimental protocols are distributed.

Ethical Considerations

This dataset was developed for scientific research on camouflaged object detection. Although some images depict military personnel or military-style camouflage patterns, the dataset does not contain classified information, tactical intelligence, or sensitive operational material. Researchers using this dataset should ensure compliance with applicable institutional, national, and international regulations regarding defense-related research.

